# Slim the P1 ground *upload* recovery kernel (images/kernel-recovery.img).
#
# Two kernels come out of the p1-gnd build. The installed one (kernel.img, in
# both .fwu bundles) runs the goggles and the Nano VRX, so it keeps the panel,
# the HDMI bridge, the decoder and the keys. This fragment is for the other
# one only: the recovery a stock unit boots from RAM through the Artosyn HID
# loader (the one-time stock->fpvOS upload, from the browser or the fpvOS
# Recovery app). That kernel only runs the firmware-update service over USB,
# then the unit reboots into the installed kernel; it never drives a screen or
# reads a key, so those subsystems are dead weight in it.
#
# The HID loader uploads at a hard ~14.6 KiB/s (full-speed, 15-byte frames), so
# this kernel's size is the wait. The outer image stays LZ4 (the vendor
# bootloader only unpacks gz/lzo/lz4); XZ only changes how the kernel stores its
# own built-in initramfs.
#
# Kept: USB gadget (DWC2/NCM/ACM/FunctionFS/configfs), MTD/spi-nand, UBI/UBIFS,
# crypto - the firmware-update path - and the P1 boot guard.
#
# Its command line is the P1 Air recovery's, with the ground units' memory:
# one CPU (the HID loader's path to a second one is not known; the stock SPL
# uses the P1 Air's secondary CPU handshake) and clk_ignore_unused (with the
# display drivers gone nothing holds their clocks, and the late clock cleanup
# stopped the P1 Air once its USB gadget was up). The installed kernel forces
# its own line (CONFIG_CMDLINE_FORCE), so the bootloader cannot pass these.
# Not run on hardware.
CONFIG_CMDLINE="console=ttyS0,1152000 earlycon loglevel=7 mem=148M rdinit=/init maxcpus=1 nr_cpus=1 clk_ignore_unused"
# NOT in any defconfig: recovery-kernel.sh applies it to a copy of the p1-gnd
# build's kernel tree (./build.sh p1-gnd recovery), so the installed kernel and
# the .fwu bundles are never slimmed.
# CONFIG_DRM is not set
# CONFIG_FB is not set
# CONFIG_BACKLIGHT_CLASS_DEVICE is not set
# CONFIG_MEDIA_SUPPORT is not set
# CONFIG_SOUND is not set
# CONFIG_SND is not set
# CONFIG_INPUT is not set
# CONFIG_HID is not set
# CONFIG_USB_HID is not set
# CONFIG_KALLSYMS is not set
# CONFIG_IKCONFIG is not set
# CONFIG_FTRACE is not set
# CONFIG_FUNCTION_TRACER is not set
# (no DEBUG_KERNEL: CONFIG_EXPERT selects it)
# CONFIG_DEBUG_FS is not set
CONFIG_RD_XZ=y
CONFIG_INITRAMFS_COMPRESSION_XZ=y
# CONFIG_INITRAMFS_COMPRESSION_GZIP is not set
